{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fibre_functor_atlas","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fibre_functor_atlas","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fibre_functor_atlas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fibre_functor_atlas","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fibre_functor_atlas.lean#L36-L56","doc":"**Proposition (fibre-functor atlas).** Let `(C, A, τ)` be a quantum\nobservable universe with `G = Aut⊗(τ)` and fibre-functor transition data\n`g` satisfying the cocycle condition. Then the four manuscript sub-claims\nhold: (i) chart identity `g(i,i) = 1`; (ii) torsor inverse\n`g(j,i) = g(i,j)⁻¹`; (iii) the cocycle condition; (iv) connectedness.\n\nClaims (i), (ii), (iv) are **derived** from the cocycle hypothesis\n`ctx.cocycle`; only (iii) restates it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:fibre-functor-atlas","label":"prop:fibre-functor-atlas","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fibre-functor-atlas.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext.cocycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext.cocycle","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fibre_functor_atlas.lean#L33-L33","doc":"**Cocycle condition** `g(i,k) = g(j,k) · g(i,j)` for every triple\n— the lone structural hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext.g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext.g","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fibre_functor_atlas.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Transition isomorphisms `g(i,j) : G` for each pair of fibre functors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext.FFIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext.FFIdx","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fibre_functor_atlas.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Fibre-functor index set (indexes the chart cover). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fibre_functor_atlas.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FibreFunctorAtlasContext","kind":"class","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fibre_functor_atlas.lean#L22-L33","doc":"Context for `fibre_functor_atlas`: the transition data `g` of a\nfibre-functor atlas over the Tannaka group `G = Aut⊗(τ)`, together with\nthe **cocycle hypothesis**, the single structural input from which the\nchart/torsor/connectedness conclusions follow. ","signatureChunk":0}]}